1. Is you radio in DFU mode?<br>Yes (red and green led flashing)<br>2. When you plug the cable is there any change in the Windows device managed ?<br>Ports and LPT: Silicon Labs CP210x USB to UART Bridge (COM4) (modified cable)<br>Universal Serial Bus Controllers: nothing showing<br>i.e If you have the wrong cable for the radio, Windows normaly displays a message to indicate a USB problem.<br>If nothing happens when you plug in the USB cable, then something is very broken, i..e the radio or the cable.<br>I have two 1701s both on Firmware 20231231192808 [140939c 1] same issue with both<br>I have two cables one modified, the other OEM Baofeng and neither work.<br>I have two laptops, both running Window 10 and have tied both without success.<br>My radios were working fine under OpenGD77. I changed nothing. Is this a Windows 10 issue?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5617">G0NQA</a> — Wed Apr 23, 2025 5:29 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
